Why this commit touches 73 files

The substantive change is 109 lines in two files:

  apps/vscode/webview-ui/src/utils/reportWebviewError.ts   (new, 33 lines)
  apps/vscode/src/core/webview/webviewLoadGuard.test.ts     (new, 76 lines)

The other ~66 files are Biome reformatting and carry no behaviour change. They were not
intended and should not be read as part of this fix.

Cause: a tooling step ran a repo-wide formatter over files it did not need to touch, and
the changes were swept into this commit instead of being left unstaged. The underlying
generator defect that prompted that step - the proto generator emitting a corrupt
`reserved` block - was fixed separately in 427b09453. No later commit in this range
carries comparable churn, so this was a one-time incident rather than a pattern.

Not cleaned up. Removing it would mean replaying the 24 commits that follow and
force-pushing a shared branch, which is a materially worse trade than a noisy diff in a
commit this far back. Recorded here instead, which annotates the commit without
rewriting history.

If you are reviewing this commit, read the two files listed above and ignore the rest.
